## Which models support document input

Per Mistral's model capability matrix, **34 models** support the "Document QnA" capability that lets you pass a document (e.g., PDF) directly in a chat message, including all current-generation chat models: Mistral Large 3/2.1, Mistral Medium 3/3.1/3.5, Mistral Small 3.0/3.1/3.2/4, Ministral 3B/8B/14B (and older Ministral 3B/8B), Magistral Medium/Small (1.0–1.2), Devstral (2, Medium, Small 1.0/1.1/2), Pixtral 12B, Pixtral Large, Voxtral Mini/Small, and Codestral (2501/2508). Notably absent from this list (vs. the general chat-completions list) are Leanstral, Mistral Nemo, Mistral Small Creative, and Z.ai GLM 5.2.

Full list: [docs.mistral.ai/models#chat-completions](https://docs.mistral.ai/models#chat-completions)

## How to pass a document

Add a content block of type `document_url` alongside your text block in the user message. You can supply it three ways:

**1. Public URL**
```python
messages = [
    {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
            {"type": "text", "text": "what is the last sentence in the document"},
            {"type": "document_url", "document_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.04770"}
        ]
    }
]
chat_response = client.chat.complete(model="mistral-small-latest", messages=messages)
```

**2. Base64-encoded PDF** (as a data URI)
```python
import base64
def encode_pdf(pdf_path):
    with open(pdf_path, "rb") as f:
        return base64.b64encode(f.read()).decode('utf-8')

base64_pdf = encode_pdf("path_to_your_pdf.pdf")
messages = [
    {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
            {"type": "text", "text": "what is the last sentence in the document"},
            {"type": "document_url", "document_url": f"data:application/pdf;base64,{base64_pdf}"}
        ]
    }
]
```

**3. Uploaded file** — upload the PDF to Mistral's cloud (same file-upload flow as OCR), retrieve a signed URL, then pass that signed URL as the `document_url` value.

Equivalent cURL:
```bash
curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${MISTRAL_API_KEY}" \
  -d '{
    "model": "mistral-small-latest",
    "messages": [{
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {"type": "text", "text": "what is the last sentence in the document"},
        {"type": "document_url", "document_url": "data:application/pdf;base64,<base64_pdf>"}
      ]
    }]
  }'
```

For a public URL, it must be publicly accessible by Mistral's API.

Source: [Document QnA — Usage](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/document-processing/document_qna#usage)

Mistral’s built-in Document Q&A support works with **all Mistral chat models**. The document is OCR-processed and the extracted content is provided to the selected model. The docs demonstrate this with `mistral-small-latest`. [Document Q&A documentation](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/document-processing/document_qna) · [Document Q&A cookbook](https://docs.mistral.ai/resources/cookbooks/mistral-ocr-document_understanding)

Pass the document as a content part in the user message, using `type: "document_url"`:

```json
{
  "model": "mistral-small-latest",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Summarize this document."
        },
        {
          "type": "document_url",
          "document_url": "https://example.com/document.pdf"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Python:

```python
messages = [{
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
        {"type": "text", "text": "Summarize this document."},
        {
            "type": "document_url",
            "document_url": "https://example.com/document.pdf",
        },
    ],
}]

response = client.chat.complete(
    model="mistral-small-latest",
    messages=messages,
)
```

The URL must be publicly accessible to Mistral’s API. For private/local files, upload the file first and pass a signed URL. The separate OCR API also supports uploaded files and Base64 documents. [OCR processor documentation](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/document-processing/basic_ocr)

